"autonomous\" run. Now recorded as **ADR-027**: deferral is `blocked` status with an evidence packet, never an unlinked backlog item.\n\n## The 202-task claim was wrong three ways\n\nIt counted owner decisions as autonomous, counted deferred work, and folded an agent build *plus an independent review cycle* into \"one short human sitting\". Simulating the live DAG with holds as barriers gives the honest shape:\n\n| | tasks |\n|---|---|\n| **Segment 1 — before any human input** | **35** |\n| C1 (permissions) + D1 → segments 2–3 | 6 |\n| **A1 (one click) → segment 4** | **164** |\n| H2+D2+D3+D4 → segment 5 | 24 |\n| C2 → segment 6 (signed/notarized release) | 13 |\n\n**245 autonomous, 8 human interactions in 5 batches.** I found a fifth mis-counted decision the reviewer hadn't named — `3mnqn8` (approving a vendored-dependency fork is an owner call).\n\n## Other review items\n\n- **C1 split**: permission grants only; the probe build and its review sit outside, then A1 is a separate single click. The residual 2FA re-prompt risk is stated, not hidden.\n- **Notarization** (ADR-025 + `TASK-260728-dveo1o`): named Keychain profile, real auth check, *and* a recorded disposition for the mode-0600 `.p8`. Corrected the canonical text that claimed notary credentials were ready.\n- **Sparkle** (ADR-026 + `TASK-260728-3bj9bk`): keygen at C1; `SUPublicEDKey` pinning and appcast verify now blocked by `uyju7n` → `xempiv` and `1mt4e7`. `ziprhs` also had literally no scope/AC — written.\n- **25 AC statements** re-scoped to macOS by exact-substring substitution (dry-run verified 25/25 first), so nothing else in any field changed. **17 obsolete iOS edges** removed only where a macOS counterpart edge survived; **4 genuine deferred-branch edges kept**.\n\n## Two things worth your attention\n\n1. **Segment 1 is only 35 tasks** because `32umrc` (generated-project ADR) is blocked by Gate P0 `2ayxqn`. I kept that edge — ADR-011 requires it and review item 5 demands P0 gates stay enforced. Removing it would make the plan look far better and be wrong. Schedule C1 early; segment 1 runs alongside arranging it.\n2. **Conditional hold X1**: `39xz9g` requires *real relux test host access* per its own scope. Nothing in the owner record confirms the agent has it. Flagged rather than assumed — if it's missing, `1u2vpc` and `297imp` stall.\n\nGates: `task-board validate` valid/0 issues, `swift test` 332/29 pass, `git diff --check` clean, product-path diff empty, invariant and secret-leak scans clean, and no `blocked` element appears anywhere in the regenerated plan.","ttft_ms":1934,"ttft_stream_ms":1415,"time_to_request_ms":19,"type":"result","duration_ms":1254514,"uuid":"e53f0801-299e-471a-8630-30c853afe05c"}
